@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki To OSB Customer Contact Role Integration
	Testing to assure koroneiki customer contact role integration to osb works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all passwords

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Kchild - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Oneiki - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Kchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Oneiki - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KCHILDKCHILD |
	| KORONEKORONE |
	| ONEIKIONEIKI |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| KCHILDKCHILD |
	| KORONEKORONE |
	| ONEIKIONEIKI |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| bso.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| bso.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Account Role     |
	| Liferay Optional Role    |
	| NonLiferay Account Role  |
	| NonLiferay Optional Role |
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Kchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Korone - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Oneiki - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Create customer contacts with roles
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Testing the ability to create customer contacts with roles on Koroneiki that later gets sent to OSB

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the Liferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                      |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the NonLiferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | NonLiferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                         |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Liferay Account Role |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| NonLiferay Account Role |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the keyword "Korone"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Team Members tab
	Then the team member with the name "OSB Koroneiki1" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Koroneiki1                       |
	| Role  | Liferay Account Role                 |
	| Email | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the team member with the name "OSB Koroneiki2" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Koroneiki2                       |
	| Role  | NonLiferay Account Role              |
	| Email | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	When I go to the Liferay Contacts tab
	Then the Liferay contact with the name "OSB Koroneiki1" should not be visible
	And the Liferay contact with the name "OSB Koroneiki2" should not be visible
	When I go to the History tab
	Then the history entry with the keywords "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki1" and "Member" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact              |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki1                |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Member                        |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki2" and "Member" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact              |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki2                |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Member                        |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki1" and "Liferay Account Role" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact              |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki1                |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Liferay Account Role          |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki2" and "NonLiferay Account Role" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact              |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki2                |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | NonLiferay Account Role       |

Scenario: Create customer contacts with roles executed by agent
	Testing the ability to create customer contacts with role assignments executed by agent on Koroneiki that later gets sent to OSB

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the Liferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                      |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the NonLiferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | NonLiferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                         |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" executed by "Koroneiki User"
	| osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles executed by "Koroneiki User"
	| Liferay Account Role |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles executed by "Koroneiki User"
	| NonLiferay Account Role |
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the keyword "Korone"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Team Members tab
	Then the team member with the name "OSB Koroneiki1" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Koroneiki1                       |
	| Role  | Liferay Account Role                 |
	| Email | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the team member with the name "OSB Koroneiki2" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Koroneiki2                       |
	| Role  | NonLiferay Account Role              |
	| Email | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	When I go to the Liferay Contacts tab
	Then the Liferay contact with the name "OSB Koroneiki1" should not be visible
	And the Liferay contact with the name "OSB Koroneiki2" should not be visible
	When I go to the History tab
	Then the history entry with the keywords "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki1" and "Member" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki User   |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki1   |
	| Update Date                 | Today            |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A              |
	| Update Field New Value      | Member           |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki2" and "Member" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki User   |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki2   |
	| Update Date                 | Today            |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A              |
	| Update Field New Value      | Member           |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki1" and "Liferay Account Role" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki User       |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact     |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki1       |
	| Update Date                 | Today                |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role         |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | Liferay Account Role |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki2" and "NonLiferay Account Role" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki User          |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact        |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki2          |
	| Update Date                 | Today                   |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role            |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                     |
	| Update Field New Value      | NonLiferay Account Role |

Scenario: Create customer contacts with nonexistent roles via nested field
	Testing the ability to create customer contacts with initially nonexistent roles on Koroneiki that later gets sent to OSB

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a nested field for a nonexistent contact role with the following values
	| Description | This is the Liferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                      |
	And I rename the first contact role nested field variable
	And I create a nested field for a nonexistent contact role with the following values
	| Description | This is the NonLiferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | NonLiferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                         |
	And I rename the second contact role nested field variable
	And I create a nested field for the customer contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the contact roles nested field value "${staticContactRolesNestedField1}"
	And I rename the first contact nested field variable
	And I create a nested field for the customer contact with the email address "osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the contact roles nested field value "${staticContactRolesNestedField2}"
	And I rename the second contact nested field variable
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORONEKORONE                                                | |
	| Contact Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken                        | |
	| Contact Nested Field  | ${staticContactsNestedField1},${staticContactsNestedField2} | |
	| Description           | Test osb account on koroneiki                               | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                                                | |
	| Name                  | Korone - ${staticProjectName}                               | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                                                | |
	| Profile Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken                        | |
	| Region                | United States                                               | |
	| Status                | Active                                                      | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                                          | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com                                | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the keyword "Korone"
	And I go to the project with the name "Korone - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Team Members tab
	Then the team member with the name "OSB Koroneiki1" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Koroneiki1                       |
	| Role  | Liferay Account Role                 |
	| Email | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the team member with the name "OSB Koroneiki2" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Koroneiki2                       |
	| Role  | NonLiferay Account Role              |
	| Email | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	When I go to the Liferay Contacts tab
	Then the Liferay contact with the name "OSB Koroneiki1" should not be visible
	And the Liferay contact with the name "OSB Koroneiki2" should not be visible
	When I go to the History tab
	Then the history entry with the keywords "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki1" and "Member" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact              |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki1                |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Member                        |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki2" and "Member" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact              |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki2                |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Member                        |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki1" and "Liferay Account Role" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact              |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki1                |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Liferay Account Role          |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Assigned Contact" and "OSB Koroneiki2" and "NonLiferay Account Role" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Koroneiki QA Service Producer |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Contact              |
	| Update Description          | OSB Koroneiki2                |
	| Update Date                 | Today                         |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | NonLiferay Account Role       |

Scenario: Create customer contacts with roles via nested field
	Testing the ability to create customer contacts with roles via nested field on Koroneiki that later gets sent to OSB

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | osb.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                  |
	| Language      | English                              |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the Liferay role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                      |
	And I create a nested field for the contact role with the name "Liferay Account Role"
	And I rename the first contact role nested field variable
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
